      "id": "S1",
      "status": "pass",
      "analysis": "FiniteOrbitSpace constructs the actual topological orbit quotient for any finite acting group on a profinite T; compactness and Hausdorffness are genuine quotient instances, and orbitTotallySeparated proves a clopen basis from quotient images of clopen sets. FiniteOrbitSheaf proves the represented quotient map locally surjective by the actual profinite pullback of a section, and its kernel is the actual covering family of finitely many closed action-graph pieces. quotientSheafIso and its factorization identify this representable quotient with the universal sheaf quotient. FreeOrbitDescent proves all-test stabilizer triviality under precisely the free action assumption, explicitly separating nonempty tests from empty tests (the empty cover enforces unique sheaf sections), then applies the canonical comparison isomorphism criterion to every equivariant sheaf. No finiteness assumption on T or representability assumption on E is added.",
