    {
      "id": "S2",
      "status": "pass",
      "analysis": "The six new fibre-classification modules construct the genuine balanced quotient Gamma times_{Gamma_t} Y with relation (g h^-1,h y)~(g,y), left action and projection, not a target-encoded certificate. OrbitFibres proves the disjoint union of induced actual fibres evaluates equivariantly and bijectively onto the original X, with the projection formula. Conversely FibreReconstruction constructs a finite object over T from every finite family of stabilizer sets, and proves the representative-fibre recovery is both bijective and stabilizer-equivariant. FibreMorphisms proves restriction and extension are inverse for every actual equivariant map over T and verifies identity/composition, with no surjectivity or nonempty-fibre requirement. FibreAutomorphisms transports stabilizers by conjugation to prove equivalence with the all-point condition and defines the actual over-T equivariant subgroup of permutations of X. It constructs a multiplicative equivalence, including inverse extension and multiplication, with the product of symmetric groups of all representative fibres. FiniteRepresentedDescent builds the actual h_X object: constant point sections prove necessity and pointwise evaluation of every section proves sufficiency for the full sheaf criterion, hence the exact realization iff. For the task finite sets the discrete profinite topology makes the displayed continuity assumptions automatic; no freeness from S1 is used. The quotient base is the represented orbit quotient by the previously proved q-compatible isomorphism. Empty fibres and the empty base are retained throughout; the symmetric group of an empty fibre is the usual trivial permutation group.",
