      "id": "S4",
      "status": "pass",
      "analysis": "PointInvisibleAction constructs a genuine RealOrbit sheaf as the sheaf quotient of the usual real-valued probe sheaf by discrete real translations. Covers of the singleton split at a chosen point, which proves its quotient section set there is a singleton. Negation descends by the universal quotient property and is proved involutive, so it defines an actual C2 action over the trivial one-point base. The Cantor probe and the continuous injective real map from the standard Cantor-set homeomorphism are actual objects. Quotient equality implies finite range of the difference by an actual finite covering family; both f and 2f have infinite range, giving an explicit nonfixed section. Thus every singleton stabilizer acts trivially but the full criterion and realization fail. The alternative use of the Cantor homeomorphism, rather than the reference ternary series, proves the same required counterexample without assuming a nontrivial section as input.",
